    title="HealthWatchApp.swift: the app's entry point",
    intro="""The iPhone app is written in Swift with SwiftUI, Apple's way of describing a screen as a function of data: you declare what should be shown for the current data, and the system redraws it whenever the data changes. The app has two long-lived objects. `BluetoothManager` talks to the watch. `HistoryStore` remembers past readings. Every screen reads from them.""",
